  <diagram id="fbfc8138313f" name="What the system does">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="960" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="2" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="1600" height="960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#173B60;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="1600" height="76" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="4" value="What the system does" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=visible;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=27;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="15" width="1470" height="47" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5" value="Backend and database walkthrough  |  Page 2" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=visible;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=12;fontColor=#526579;fontStyle=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="907" width="1450" height="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="6" value="DRRAS helps a coordinator decide how many ambulances each resource base could send to each affected area in a simulated disaster. The inputs are the scenario, the locations of its bases and areas, the number of ambulances at each base, and the demand and severity of each area. The output is a set of proposed assignments and measures the coordinator can compare. Population is recorded and displayed. Demand is entered explicitly by the coordinator." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=16;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="118" width="1480" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7" value="A typical demonstration goes through these steps:" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=16;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="227" width="1480" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8" value="1. Open the dashboard and select a sample. In Scenario data, show the severity-colored areas and the base markers. Each base has its own stock and each area has its own demand." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=15;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="289" width="1480" height="46" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9" value="2. In Allocations, run the baseline. The first run requests road times from OSRM and stores one matrix row for each base and area pair. When OSRM cannot supply a pair, DRRAS saves an estimated time for that pair and labels it." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=15;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="349" width="1480" height="68" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10" value="3. Run the optimizer. It reads the same matrix and the original stock. Both runs record assignments, metrics, and runtime in the database." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=15;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="431" width="1480" height="46" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="11" value="4. Open Compare results to see the two maps and the metric differences. The difference is optimized minus baseline. A smaller travel cost and a larger coverage ratio are generally desirable. One method may improve some measures while worsening others." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=15;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="492" width="1480" height="68" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="12" value="5. Refresh the browser and show that the results are still there. Add or remove an area or a base, then show that the dashboard requires fresh runs for the updated scenario. The previous runs remain in API history." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D5E1EB;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#172B42;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=15;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="574" width="1480" height="68" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
